  "response": "**Step 1: Count integers divisible by 3 or 5 (1–1000)**\n\nUsing inclusion-exclusion:\n- Divisible by 3: ⌊1000/3⌋ = 333\n- Divisible by 5: ⌊1000/5⌋ = 200\n- Divisible by 15 (3∩5): ⌊1000/15⌋ = 66\n\nDivisible by 3 or 5 = 333 + 200 − 66 = **467**\n\n**Step 2: Subtract those also divisible by 7**\n\nI need to remove numbers that are divisible by 7 **and** (divisible by 3 or 5) — i.e., divisible by 21 or by 35.\n\n- Divisible by 21 (7∩3): ⌊1000/21⌋ = 47\n- Divisible by 35 (7∩5): ⌊1000/35⌋ = 28\n- Divisible by 105 (7∩3∩5, lcm(21,35)=105): ⌊1000/105⌋ = 9\n\nDivisible by 21 or 35 = 47 + 28 − 9 = **66**\n\n**Step 3: Final count**\n\nNumbers divisible by 3 or 5, but not by 7 = 467 − 66 = **401**\n\nFINAL ANSWER: 401",
